h"] " of Germany, with Hungarian defending gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/103582"} "Dániel Gyurta"] " also formidable. Then American " [:a {:href "/athletes/136364"} "Josh Prenot"] ", just out of college, won the US Olympic Trials in 2:07.17, an American record and the second fastest time in history, and brought himself into the conversation. By the start of the Rio Olympics, there was no obvious favorite."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Not discussed among even the medal contenders was Kazakh swimmer " [:a {:href "/athletes/134858"} "Dmitry Balandin"] ", but he won the gold medal in major upset with Prenot taking silver, as Balandin set a national record of 2:07.46. Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/135799"} "Anton Chupkov"] " took the bronze in another surprise, posting another national record of 2:07.70. Koch finished seventh in the final, while Gyurta failed to even make the semi-finals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Balandin, the 2014 Asian Games Champion, became the first swimmer in 20 years to win Olympic gold from lane eight, after Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45268"} "Kieren Perkins"] " in the 1,500 freestyle. Balandin’s gold medal was the first ever medal for Kazakhstan in swimming."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134858"} "Dmitry Balandin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KAZ"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KAZ.png"}] "KAZ"]] [:td {} "2:09.00 (3 h4)"] [:td {} "2:08.20 (4 h1)"] [:td {} "2:07.46 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136364"} "Josh Prenot"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle",